   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">High-level platform(s) for political dialogue and consensus building on federal framework and IGR are established and activated including the commencement of (Interim) Inter-State Commission. 
# of high-level dialogues organized.
# of Regional Reconciliation Plans (RRPs)  
# of Operational Manuals 
# of ToTs on Insider Mediation conducted 
# of elders trained on insider mediation 
# of communal conflicts resolved</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Political agreements on key issues shaping the federal framework and mechanism for intergovernmental relations(IGR) management have not been achieved yet. 

National Reconciliation Framework (NRF) has been developed albeit with limited ownership by all stakeholders particularly FMSs and traditional elders. 

Primary data on conflict mapping has been collected to be incorporated in the regional reconciliation plans.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">At least one National Summit on Federalism and 2 inter-ministerial meetings and on Master Class on IGR dialogue organized
Four high level advocacy meetings/consultations are conducted for the adoption of Formalisation Report on boundary delimitation of FMSes
At least 2 Regional Reconciliation Plans are developed 

At least 30 elders are trained on insider mediation 
At least 3 community reconciliation interventions conducted and peace agreements achieved</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Federalist governance model strengthened and National Reconciliation Framework (NRF) implemented</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
